SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ppoollll() function conforms to IEEE Std 1003.1-2001 (“POSIX.1”).  The
     ppppoollll() is not specified by POSIX.  The POLLRDHUP flag is not specified
     by POSIX, but is compatible with Linux and illumos.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppoollll() function appeared in AT&T System V UNIX.  This manual page and
     the core of the implementation was taken from NetBSD.  The ppppoollll() func‐
     tion first appeared in FreeBSD 11.0

BBUUGGSS
     The distinction between some of the fields in the _e_v_e_n_t_s and _r_e_v_e_n_t_s bit‐
     masks is really not useful without STREAMS.  The fields are defined for
     compatibility with existing software.

